SPL -- the print spooler's queue directory==========================================splman (the manager), splprt (the printer process) and splstat (the statusreport) all open /DD/SPL/splq.  Without the directory and the file they eachstopped at error 216, path-not-found, and said nothing.splq is here and EMPTY: an empty queue is the correct state for a spoolerwith nothing to print.THE CLIENTS WANT A MODULE, NOT A FILE, and that is as far as this goes.`lpq', `prjob' and `lp' look for a DATA MODULE called `spoolqueue' inmemory and answer `no spooler installed' when it is not there.  Starting`splman &' does not create it -- splman runs, as a daemon should, and lpqstill says no spooler.  Whatever builds `spoolqueue' is not on this disk.Measured 2026-08-29.